  "output": "We are given: \"Zaid spends 1/4 of his salary on rent, 1/3 on car fuel and donates half of the remaining amount to his favorite charity. He gives his daughter 200$ to use for her weekly expenses and 700$ to his wife to budget for groceries and other household goods. If Zaid earns 6000$ per month, how much money will he still have after all these expenses and donations?\"\n\nWe need to compute step by step.\n\nFirst, total salary = 6000$.\n\nSpending:\n- Rent: 1/4 of salary = (1/4)*6000 = 1500$.\n- Car fuel: 1/3 of salary = (1/3)*6000 = 2000$.\n\nSo total spent on rent and car fuel = 1500 + 2000 = 3500$.\n\nRemaining after rent and car fuel: 6000 - 3500 = 2500$.\n\nThen, he donates half of the remaining amount to his favorite charity. So donation = (1/2)*2500 = 1250$.\n\nSo after rent, car fuel, and charity donation, he has: 2500 - 1250 = 1250$.\n\nThen he gives his daughter 200$ and his wife 700$ to budget for groceries and other household goods. So total given to family = 200 + 700 = 900$.\n\nSo money left after all these: 1250 - 900 = 350$.\n\nThus, he will still have 350$.\n\nCheck: 6000 - 1500 - 2000 - 1250 - 200 - 700 = 6000 - (1500+2000+1250+200+700) = 6000 - (3500+1250+900) = 6000 - (4750+900) = 6000 - 5650 = 350. Yes.\n\nSo final answer: 350.\n\nWe need to output: FINAL: 350\n\nBut the instruction says: \"End your response with a separate line in exactly this format: FINAL: <integer>.\" So we should write the final line as \"FINAL: 350\".\n\nLet's double-check the problem statement: \"Zaid spends 1/4 of his salary on rent, 1/3 on car fuel and donates half of the remaining amount to his favorite charity. He gives his daughter 200$ to use for her weekly expenses and 700$ to his wife to budget for groceries and other household goods.\" So the order: first rent, then car fuel, then donation, then daughter, then wife. That's what we did.\n\nAll good.</think>Zaid's total salary is 6000$.  \n- Rent: 1/4 × 6000 = 1500$  \n- Car fuel: 1/3 × 6000 = 2000$  \n- Total spent on rent and fuel: 1500 + 2000 = 3500$  \n- Remaining after rent and fuel: 6000 - 3500 = 2500$  \n- Donation to charity: half of remaining = 1/2 × 2500 = 1250$  \n- Money left after donation: 2500 - 1250 = 1250$  \n- Given to daughter: 200$  \n- Given to wife: 700$  \n- Total given to family: 200 + 700 = 900$  \n- Final money: 1250 - 900 = 350$\n\nFINAL: 350",
